# Every tool the gate runs, pinned by version: this file is the only place one is written.
# Each is run with `go run <module>@<version>`: go checks the module against go's checksum
# database (the private gragas module against GOPRIVATE, by the clone's own git login), so
# a pin here is a version and nothing is installed on the machine.
#
# This file is data, never shell: gate/read-pins.sh reads it, and the hooks and the `pins`
# member refuse any line that is not a comment, a blank or one of the four below, each once.
#
# GOTOOLCHAIN is the pinned Go: every `go run` of the hooks and the Taskfile gets it, so the
# runner, gitleaks and gragas are built by this Go on every machine, not by the first one on the path.
# GRAGAS_PIN is the pinned gragas: a commit of birdtable/gragas release-1 (not main, until
# release 1 ships: `plugin test` is built there), read by a reviewer as one line. The names
# scan, `plugin test` (C1 to C4, C6 and C18 to C22 run today; C5, C7 to C17 and C23 wait for the
# wasm host, and C5 and C7 to C13 also for a later part of it, by a later move of
# this pin) and `plugin contract --json` run from this same pin.
# Move it only in a pull request that says why. A tagged release replaces the commit when
# gragas has one.
GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.27.4
TASK_PIN=v3.54.0
GITLEAKS_PIN=v8.30.1
GRAGAS_PIN=537e9e2f4d0d947d0034ebd093cfd35940da5447
